!Tune
=====

Example 6: plays three notes, left, middle and right, through OpenAL. No window; it takes about two seconds.

Built from sound.c in the riscos-mesa devkit's examples folder; read the
comments in that file to see how it works.

Needs: RISC OS 5, an ARMv7 or later processor (Raspberry Pi 2, 3 or 4,
or a Cortex-A8/A9/A15 board), and SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport
from PackMan.

For sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager, or else DigitalRenderer.
(SharedSound is part of RISC OS; only these two need installing.)
  Download: the ssb.zip download on Andrew Sellors' RDPClient page,
    https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html
    Merge its !System into yours.
  Background: John Duffell's own site (now on the Internet Archive) has
    more details:
    https://web.archive.org/web/20110920080106/http://www.duffell.riscos.me.uk/

